<h2>STANDARD TERMS &amp; CONDITIONS:</h2><h4>Booking &amp; Payment Procedure</h4>
						<ul class="terms-content">                    
						<li style="list-style: disc;">25% of the ticket value as an advance at the time of booking, along with the list of guests/pax and their scanned soft copies of passports. </li><li style="list-style: disc;">Balance payment is due 90 days prior to the departure date. </li><li style="list-style: disc;">In the case of bookings made within 90 days prior to the departure date, 100% payment shall be deposited to the authorized O&M operator along with the booking details. </li><li style="list-style: disc;">The rate of exchange prevailing on the date of the transaction will be applicable as per the Reserve Bank of India (India's Central Bank). </li><li style="list-style: disc;">5% GST (or as applicable) at time of payment, shall be charged extra. </li><li style="list-style: disc;">The tariff for a child aged up to 5 years will not be charged. The tariff for a child aged above 5 years but less than 12 years shall be charged at 50%, in the same Deluxe cabin with the parents.</li><li style="list-style: disc;">Usage of bar facilities is chargeable as per actuals. </li><li style="list-style: disc;">Timing & departure schedule can be changed based on weather conditions, technical issues, or force majeure.</li><li style="list-style: disc;"> One cabin has an occupancy of 2 Adults only (On special request a child below 12 years can be accommodated in the same Deluxe cabin). </li><li style="list-style: disc;">The tariff in Indian currency is fixed for guests having valid Indian nationality proof, i.e., a valid Indian passport and OCI card holders (valid proof for the same needs to be submitted at the time of booking. In case of any variance in the documents, the dollar rate would be applicable).</li>          </ul>          <h4>Cancellation Rules for Deduction of amount</h4>          <ul class="terms-content">           <li style="list-style: disc;">25% of ticket value shall be deducted on cancellation prior to 90 days before the travel date. </li><li style="list-style: disc;">50% of ticket value shall be deducted on cancellation between 89 to 60 days before the travel date. </li><li style="list-style: disc;">75% of the ticket value shall be deducted on cancellation around 59 to 30 days before the travel date </li><li style="list-style: disc;">No refund shall be admissible in case the booking is cancelled within 29 days before the departure date. </li><li style="list-style: disc;">Operator reserves the right to cancel the tour/trips at any given point of time to whatsoever reasons. On cancellation of booking suo-moto by Operator, the fund deposited (without any claims) will be refunded, after deducting 10% Travel agent service charges. No refund of GST or Convenience fee will be applicable.</li>  <li style="list-style: disc;">Travellers shall be provided an option for an amendment/shifting of seats free of cost available on the next tours.</li>  <li style="list-style: disc;">Operator will not be liable for any refund or compensation for any services such as pre/post accommodation, airline tickets, and excursions etc. that have been booked by the guest and/or his/her Travel Agent. </li><li style="list-style: disc;">Operator will review and apprise the agents of such instances 60 days prior to departure in case of low occupancy.</li><li style="list-style: disc;">Operator has the right to decide the same between 45 days to 30 days of the departure and officially inform the agents or individuals of such bookings. </li><li style="list-style: disc;">The minimum occupancy defined is of 50% to run the operations, that is 17 cabins.</li>          </ul>          <h4>Part Journey</h4> <ul class="terms-content"> <li style="list-style: disc;">For already existing bookings, the operator will accommodate them, but for new bookings, part bookings will be entertained only at the discretion of the RTDC operator based on occupancy. </li> <li style="list-style: disc;">New bookings will be made only for the full itinerary, i.e., 7 nights. In case any guest leaves en route during the trip/journey, no amount will be refunded or claimed by them in any form as per the policy.</li>          </ul>          <h4>Procedure for confirmed bookings-</h4>          <ul class="terms-content">          <li style="list-style: disc;">In the case of all confirmed bookings, they shall be confirmed only upon the deposition of 100% of the ticket value along with the Passenger List/Passport scan copy 90 days prior to the travel date. If the Passenger List/Passport scan copy is not received 90 days prior to the travel date, the booking shall be treated as cancelled and no refund will be admissible. </li><li style="list-style: disc;">Once the names of the guests have been received, no substitution shall be permitted. The previous name, if changed/removed, shall be treated as a cancelled booking. The new name(s) will be treated as a fresh booking and will be confirmed based on availability. </li>  </ul>  <h4>No Show/ EnRoute Termination of Tour</h4>          <ul class="terms-content">         <li style="list-style: disc;">No Show: In case of no show/non-arrival of the guest, no refund or adjustment for future travel will be possible. The whole amount shall be treated as forfeited. However, under circumstances like Natural Disaster/Natural Calamity, the matter will be favourably considered by the Authorized Operator to the extent of Tourist/Passengers' satisfaction and their comfort for a better luxury travel experience and related promotions. </li><li style="list-style: disc;">En Route Termination of Tour: In case of termination of the tour by the guest, for any reason, no refund or adjustment for future travel will be admissible. The amount for the unused portion of the tour shall be treated as forfeited.</li>          </ul>
